    "body": "The current form is actually preferable, at least for now and in HTML. **this** technically only has meaning, currently, in ES-style algorithms, so we've been trying to use \"this X object\" or \"this element\" instead.\n\nEventually we may have Web IDL define the `this` keyword to mean \"the Web IDL object corresponding to the JavaScript object given by `this`\" or something like that.\n",
